refactor(engine): stop registering the modules — @our/prompt-modules loads them

The prompt modules are now registered by a separate, minimal plugin that reads the
definitions file and hands them to the harness. That plugin is built to be dull and
does not chase upstream, which is the point: the prompt content no longer depends on
this plugin loading at all.

Registering them in BOTH places would not merely duplicate work — dsh refuses a
duplicate section name within a scope ("prompt section X is already registered"),
so the second registration would throw.

What stays here is the DIGEST: the dirty check still tracks the definitions' current
state, so the panel knows when an edit is waiting on the next turn. The disposers map
existed only for these registrations and is gone with them.